The 2026-11-06 wording sweep report (https://claude.ai/artifact/UKKhGdhBUbrcjPooPtcsDL) found 40 problems. On "build it" only the 6 he had agreed in comments were built (squash d7975301fd). He then ran the app on staging, saw the sign-up heading/button mismatch (report item 26, already found) and asked why the sweep "missed those obvious places". I had also told him the mismatch didn't come from my sweep, without saying the sweep had found it.

The "about 100 messages" line was a real miss: it was on the first-launch screens, which the brief marked as already reviewed, and an earlier review had chosen that wording. The cold-reader method only sees screenshots, so it can't tell a clear sentence is wrong or incomplete; numbers and claims need a check against their source (server config, code).

**Why:** a proposal left unbuilt looks exactly like a miss once he runs the app.

**How to apply:** when building only part of a report, say in the same message how many found problems stay on screen and list them. When he reports a problem, first check whether a report already has it and say so. In a sweep, check every number and factual claim on screen against its source, including screens marked as already reviewed. Related: [[cold-reader-agent-catches-cryptic-ui-text]], [[label-current-proposed-agreed]].
