<!-- ============ HOME ============ -->
<h2 id="home">Home</h2>
<p class="sub">Sam has a P1S printing, a Tape dispenser printed yesterday, and a project whose G-code was exported for an Ender.</p>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/home-projects.webp" alt="Home project cards: arrow_headband printing, Tape dispenser printed, find_my_hollow marked Draft" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Home, project cards</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>A project whose G-code was exported is called a draft</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">find_my_hollow</q> … <q class="ui">Draft</q>, while print history shows <q class="ui">✓ Exported find_my_hollow.gcode</q>.</dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>"Draft" means the project was never sliced or finished. The person exported it and may have printed it from a card, so the card contradicts the history page.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd>When the latest G-code was exported and not sent: <q class="ui">G-code exported Nov 3 for Ender-3 V3 KE</q>. Keep "Draft" only for projects with no G-code.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp</code> <code>ledger_text</code> has three cases: "Printed", "Sent", and "Draft" for everything else. Export is not a case.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span></dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/home-projects.webp" alt="Tape dispenser card with the link Tell us how it printed · 25 credits" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Same cards, Tape dispenser</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>The report invitation joins an action and a reward with a dot</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">Tell us how it printed · 25 credits</q> (also a button on each print-history entry).</dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>The dot reads as a price: telling costs 25 credits. A person who does read it as a reward doesn't know what a credit buys.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd><q class="ui">Share how it printed and get 25 credits</q>. Kenneth noted that "report" sounds like reporting an app bug. "Rate" would undersell the form, which asks for a photo and 200 characters, so "share" fits better. The form's title, <q class="ui">Tell us how it printed</q>, can stay.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>HomeUI/src/history.ts</code> <code>REPORT_OFFER</code>. The reward is <code>REPORT_CREDITS</code>, paid for a sent report, so "get" is true.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span> (partly: it asked what a credit is worth)</dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/home-printers.webp" alt="Ender card: 1 G-code · never printed" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Home, printer cards</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>"Never printed" says something the app can't know</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">1 G-code · never printed</q> on the Ender card, and <q class="ui">Exported once · never printed</q> on project cards and in the project pane.</dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>The print failed or the file is broken. In fact, someone who exported G-code to a card and printed it from the printer's screen is told they never printed.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd><q class="ui">1 G-code, never sent to a printer</q> and <q class="ui">Exported once, never sent to a printer</q>. This is true because JusPrin records every G-code it sends.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>HomeUI/src/history.ts:61</code> and <code>:97</code>, <code>Shell/LeftPaneProject.cpp:316</code>. These lines count only prints the app sent or watched. An export is recorded but the print from the card is not.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span> (it asked why the file exists if it never printed)</dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/home-menu.webp" alt="Printer menu: Connect…, Printer settings…, Calibrate…, Rename, Remove printer…" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Home, the Ender's … menu</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>"Printer settings…" opens a chat, not settings</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">Printer settings…</q>. In the main window's filament menu, <q class="ui">Filament settings…</q> does the same.</dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>A settings window will open. A chat panel opens instead, and Orca's settings window is one step further inside it.</dd>
    <dt>Agreed</dt><dd class="agreed">Have both. <q class="ui">Printer settings…</q> opens the settings window, and a new item under it, <q class="ui">Ask AI about printer settings…</q>, opens the chat. The same goes for <q class="ui">Filament settings…</q> and <q class="ui">Ask AI about filament settings…</q>.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>OrcaHomeBackend::open_printer_settings</code> opens the printer's conversation. <code>Shell/FilamentMenu.cpp:470</code> calls <code>open_filament_help</code>, which opens the filament panel in the printer panel.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag own">Only my reading</span> (the cold reader asked whether it meant the profile or the connection)</dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/home-printers.webp" alt="P1S card with Launch monitor button" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Home, P1S card</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>One button, two names, and neither says what opens</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">Launch monitor</q> on a Bambu printer, <q class="ui">Open printer window</q> on a Klipper or OctoPrint printer.</dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>"Monitor" might be a camera, another app, or a screen. Both cold readers that saw Home asked.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd><q class="ui">Open printer window</q> on both. Each opens one window for that printer.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>OrcaHomeBackend::launch_monitor</code> opens the printer's monitor window, or the print host's window for a named printer. <code>PrinterCard.tsx:184</code> picks the label.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span></dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<!-- ============ HISTORY ============ -->
<h2 id="history">Print history</h2>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/hist-top.webp" alt="History entry with the code 7c1e 9a40 after the file name" loading="lazy"><img src="img/spec-062.webp" alt="Chat marker: Plate 1 · a71f 8c04 → Bambu X1C · Oct 1" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Print history entry; the G-code marker in a chat</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>Each G-code carries a code nobody can read</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">arrow_headband_plate_1.gcode 7c1e 9a40</q>, <q class="ui">Tape dispenser_plate_1.gcode · b4f2 0c77 → Bambu Lab P1S</q> on the report form, and <q class="ui">Plate 1 · a71f 8c04 → Bambu X1C · Oct 1</q> in a chat.</dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>A version, an error code, or something to act on. Three cold readers called it meaningless.</dd>
    <dt>Agreed</dt><dd class="agreed">Remove the code from every screen: history entries, the report form and the chat's G-code marker. It stays for internal use only.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd>The code is the start of the G-code's content hash, shown by <code>PrintHistory.tsx</code> and the chat's G-code marker.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span></dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/hist-yesterday.webp" alt="Two Tape dispenser entries: one Finished, one Started with no end and File no longer kept" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Print history, yesterday's two prints</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>A print the app didn't see finish reads as stuck or failed</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">Started · Bambu Lab P1S 14:12 →</q> with nothing after the arrow, while the Home card says <q class="ui">2 prints · finished yesterday</q>.</dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>"Did it fail? Did I cancel it?" The arrow promises an end time that never comes.</dd>
    <dt>Agreed</dt><dd class="agreed">Say nothing about an outcome JusPrin doesn't know. For this print, show only <q class="ui">Sent to Bambu Lab P1S at 14:11</q>, with no "Started" line and no arrow. The same rule removes <q class="ui">last print failed</q> and <q class="ui">last print cancelled</q> from the Home printer card. My reading, not yet confirmed: "Printing" and "Finished" stay on prints JusPrin watched to the end, because there it knows them.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>PrintHistory.tsx:90</code> shows "Started" for a print with no reported finish. The comment in <code>history.ts</code> records the 2026-10-27 decision never to say a print failed. The printer card's "last print failed" comes from <code>LastPrint::Failed</code> in <code>OrcaHomeBackend.cpp:263</code>, shown by <code>PrinterCard.tsx:42</code>.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span></dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/hist-yesterday.webp" alt="File no longer kept · slice again to print it" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Same entry, right of the report button</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>"Slice again" with nothing to press</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">File no longer kept · slice again to print it</q>, with no slice or open button on the entry.</dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>The app deleted their file, and they have to find out where slicing happens.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd><q class="ui">This G-code is no longer kept. Open the project and slice it to print it again.</q> The project name at the top of the entry is already a link to the project.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>PrintHistory.tsx</code> <code>printAgainNote</code>. No slice action exists on the entry.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span></dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/hist-yesterday.webp" alt="Sent to Bambu Lab P1S 19:32 · on the printer's SD · started" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Same entries, the "Sent" line</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>The "Sent" line repeats the status line and adds plumbing</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">Sent to Bambu Lab P1S 19:32 · on the printer's SD · started</q>, followed by <q class="ui">Finished · Bambu Lab P1S 19:34 → 21:40</q>.</dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>They have to care about the SD card (is it full?), and "started" appears twice.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd><q class="ui">Sent to Bambu Lab P1S at 19:32.</q> Say where the file went only when it matters, for example when it was not started.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>PrintHistory.tsx:61</code> adds "on the printer's SD" and "started" or "not started".</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span></dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/home-report.webp" alt="Report form showing 0 of 200 characters" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Report form</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>A minimum length reads as a maximum</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">0 of 200 characters</q> under <q class="ui">What happened, in a few sentences</q>.</dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>They may write up to 200 characters. In fact they must write at least 200 before Send turns on, and "a few sentences" is shorter than that.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd><q class="ui">Write at least 200 characters (0 so far).</q> Also say what unlocks Send: a photo, an outcome and the text.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>PrintReportForm.tsx:49</code>: Send needs a photo, an outcome and <code>length &gt;= REPORT_MIN_TEXT</code> (200). The hint at <code>:103</code> shows only while under it.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span>. It also asked who sees the photo; the form doesn't say.</dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<!-- ============ PROJECT CHAT ============ -->
<h2 id="chat">Project chat (the Agent page)</h2>
<p class="sub">These are crops from the page's own state gallery, so the chat content in them is sample text. The problems are in the app's fixed text, not the samples.</p>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/spec-002.webp" alt="The native host did not answer the hello handshake" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The panel when it can't start</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>A start-up failure in developer words</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">The native host did not answer the hello handshake.</q></dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>Nothing useful. The cold reader also had no next step once Retry failed.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd><q class="ui">The AI chat didn't start. Try again, and restart JusPrin if it keeps happening.</q> Keep the original sentence inside Diagnostics.</dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>WebShared/bridgeClient.ts:140</code>, set when the host doesn't answer within the timeout.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span></dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/spec-012.webp" alt="Delete dialog with Wait for the current action to finish before deleting" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Delete dialog while the chat is busy</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>Two different sentences block the same delete, and one names hidden "pending actions"</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd>The dialog: <q class="ui">Wait for the current action to finish before deleting.</q> The banner when the host refuses: <q class="ui">Finish or stop the reply and resolve pending actions before deleting this chat.</q></dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>"What action? Nothing looks pending." Nothing on screen shows what to resolve.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd>One sentence for both: <q class="ui">This chat is still working. Stop it or let it finish, then delete it.</q></dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>ChatNavigation.tsx:323</code> and <code>Agent/AgentHost.cpp:2333</code>. The cold reader saw a shorter test version of the banner, but the real one has the same problem.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span></dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/spec-011.webp" alt="Delete dialog: Your model and print history will stay" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Delete dialog</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>"Model" here could mean the AI model</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">Delete ‘Strong print’ and its messages? Your model and print history will stay. This cannot be undone.</q></dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>Inside a chat, "model" may mean the AI model. The sentence also doesn't say whether the settings the chat changed stay.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd><q class="ui">Delete ‘Strong print’ and its messages? Your project and its print history stay as they are. This can't be undone.</q></dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>ChatNavigation.tsx:322</code>. <code>AgentHost.cpp:2339</code> removes the conversation from the chat record and touches nothing in the project.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span></dd>
  </dl></div>
</section>

<section class="problem">
  <figure><img src="img/spec-070.webp" alt="Earlier chat notice: There have been project updates since this chat" loading="lazy"><img src="img/spec-074.webp" alt="Restore dialog with a raw timestamp" loading="lazy"><figcaption>An earlier chat, then its restore dialog</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="body"><h3>Going back to an earlier chat hides what restoring does, and shows a machine timestamp</h3><dl>
    <dt>On screen</dt><dd><q class="ui">There have been project updates since this chat. Restore its saved project version to continue.</q> Then the dialog: <q class="ui">Restore “Quick print” from 2026-10-03T12:00:00Z? Its earlier model and settings will replace the working version, with the matching intent and plan. Your current version will remain in history.</q></dd>
    <dt>What they think</dt><dd>The notice doesn't say their current work gets replaced. The dialog's time doesn't match the "Saved Oct 3" on the card, and "intent and plan" is internal language.</dd>
    <dt>Proposal</dt><dd>Notice: <q class="ui">The project has changed since this chat. To continue here, JusPrin puts the project back the way it was then.</q> Dialog: <q class="ui">Put the project back to Oct 3, 5:00 AM? Your current version stays in Version history.</q></dd>
    <dt>Code</dt><dd><code>App.tsx:415</code> and <code>:745</code>. <code>savedAt</code> is written by <code>Workspace/UtcTime.hpp</code> as <code>%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ</code> and shown as is. The same raw time goes into the "Ask current chat" draft at <code>App.tsx:426</code>. "Remains in history" is true: <code>AgentHost.cpp</code> checkpoints the active chat before restoring.</dd>
    <dt>Caught by</dt><dd><span class="tag cr">Cold reader caught it</span></dd>
  </dl></div>
